# Material case contradictions

Flag only **gotcha lies**: the same claim stated two different ways in a way that can win the case.

**Flag:** two filings give different interest rates, monthly payments, amounts owed, fee totals, first-default dates, 90-day/notice dates, or foreclosure-filing dates; a filing says an exhibit is attached and that exhibit is not in the case; arithmetic on a statement does not add up.

**Do not flag:** mortgage dated vs recorded; origination vs recording; Bank of America in a pleading vs an insurer or different servicer on an exhibit; WaMu / Washington Mutual; same month, different day; NYSCEF header dates; counsel letterhead; party-name lists that simply do not overlap.

A dated mortgage in 2006 and a recorded mortgage in 2009 is chronology, not a contradiction.
